  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d4ecd1a615a340f4c9104ca01624d106, type: 3}
  m_Name: FullTrack
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::YourCall.Dilemma
  _id: full_track
  _verb: 4
  _weight: 2
  _narratorPrompt: Last one, and I have taken away your favourite toy. No empty rail. Three tracks, all occupied, and the cart is already rolling, so doing nothing is only a slower way of choosing. On the first track, a child. On the second, a woman heavy with [amber]one[/amber] more life she has not met yet. On the third, [amber]three[/amber] grown strangers, three whole people. Innocence, or the most lives, or the [amber]two[/amber] who have barely lived at all. Every switch is a [red]killing[/red]. Point it somewhere. Your call.
  _choices:
  - _id: child
    _label: The child
    _narratorReact: You sent it at the child. The smallest, the newest, the one with the most mornings still owed to it, and you spent every one of them to keep a woman and [amber]three[/amber] strangers. The most life saved, you will say. The most life [red]ended[/red], someone else will say. You are both right, which is exactly why I asked.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: top
    _gambledParty:
    _route: up
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 12
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
  - _id: woman
    _label: The woman
    _narratorReact: You sent it at the woman, and the one she was carrying goes with her, [amber]two[/amber] [red]folded[/red] for the price of a single flinch. You spared a child and [amber]three[/amber] strangers and told yourself that was the larger number. Perhaps it was. You will simply never meet the person you rounded down to nothing to get there.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: mid
    _gambledParty:
    _route: straight
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 27
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: 1
    - _axis: 2
      _value: -1
  - _id: three
    _label: The three
    _narratorReact: You sent it at the three. The biggest heap of bodies on the board, chosen so one child and one unborn stranger could carry on. You picked innocence over arithmetic and called [amber]three[/amber] [red]deaths[/red] the gentle option. It might even be. I simply enjoy that you had to become a small [red]massacre[/red] to protect the sweetest two here.
    _narratorReactStruck:
    _struckParty: bottom
    _gambledParty:
    _route: down
    _diverts: 0
    _seedVotes: 61
    _endsGame: 0
    _profileImpact:
    - _axis: 0
      _value: -1
  _mainFigureCount: 3
  _spurFigureCount: 1
  _figuresBranded: 0
